        "event": "Flood Watch",
        "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
        "senderName": "NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 16 at 4:51AM EDT until August 16 at 12:00PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of western Maryland, including the following\nareas, Central and Eastern Allegany and Extreme Western Allegany\nand eastern West Virginia, including the following areas, Eastern\nGrant, Eastern Mineral, Hampshire, Hardy, Western Grant and\nWestern Mineral.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon EDT today.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Low-water\ncrossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- A cluster of thunderstorms producing very heavy rain is\napproaching the area from southeast Ohio and northern West\nVirginia. These thunderstorms have been producing rainfall\namounts of 2 to 3 inches per hour. These storms may affect\nparts of the area this morning, resulting in similar rainfall\namounts and a risk for flash flooding.\n- Please visit www.weather.gov/safety/flood for flood safety\nand preparedness information.",
        "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "note": null,
