        "senderName": "NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 16 at 4:51AM EDT until August 17 at 12:00AM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of western Maryland, including the following\nareas, Eastern Garrett and Western Garrett.\n\n* WHEN...Through this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Multiple rounds of showers and thunderstorms are expected,\nwith the first round starting around or shortly before\ndaybreak, and the final round ending by late this evening. A\nwidespread 1 to 2 inches of rain is expected, with localized\ntotals of 3 to 5 inches possible where heavier thunderstorms\nmove through. Given saturated soils after recent rainfall,\nsome instances of flash flooding may occur. Considerable\nflash flooding is possible if the heaviest rainfall amounts\noccur over areas that saw the heaviest rain recently.\n- Please visit www.weather.gov/safety/flood for flood safety\nand preparedness information.",
        "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
